# Cloudflare Pages redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Deliberately minimal. Two rules that are NOT here, and must not come back:
#
#   /* /index.html 200      A rule matches BEFORE the static asset lookup, so
#                           this proxied every hashed JS/CSS chunk, every image
#                           and robots.txt itself to index.html. Not needed:
#                           with no 404.html in the build, Pages already serves
#                           index.html for any unmatched path, which is the SPA
#                           fallback the react-router deep links rely on.
#
#   /admin /admin.html 200  Sent /admin into an infinite redirect on the first
#                           real deploy: the rule rewrote /admin to /admin.html,
#                           then Pages' own canonicalisation 308'd that back to
#                           /admin, matching the rule again. Also not needed —
#                           that same canonicalisation serves admin.html at
#                           /admin for free. (`npm run dev` has no such
#                           behaviour, which is what the adminEntryRewrite
#                           plugin in vite.config.js is for.)
#
# What remains: the prerendered per-route files are flat (stories/<slug>.html
# served at /stories/<slug>). Pages documents placeholders here, but not what
# it does with an unmatched trailing slash, so those two are explicit.
/stories/:slug/    /stories/:slug    301
/more/:slug/       /more/:slug       301
